You rush to the cage, pulling out branches locking its door. Snoopy puts his paws on your shoulders, trying to lick your face.
"Wait, boy, not now," you push him away.
Finally, the cage is opened. It's dangerous to stay here any longer; most likely, the savages will get brave enough to return soon. You run into the forest, in the opposite direction the savages ran.
Soon, the clearing of savages is left far behind. You have no idea where to run next, and your recent deed seems to you total madness now. But looking at the happy Snoopy running by your side, you come to the conclusion that even crazy deeds have their uses sometimes.